{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '6\\\\.3|6\\\\.4|8\\\\.1|P4′|php/run-main|oracle' docs/design/yang.preludes.md && ls -a\"","aggregated_output":"15:- **2026-11-21 (r7 → r8 reconciliation):** Addressed all findings from the r7 architect review (thread `01a1faa3-bb7e-7c30-b3bf-cedbad008bfc`; 8 HIGH, 1 MEDIUM, plus default-profile regressions): (H1) explicit default-selector mechanism — the composition's immutable configuration carries the preferred `[id revision]`, applied at the normal request entry, with two-revision / legacy-pin / in-flight-snapshot gates; (H2) per-frontend **entry-lowering contracts** emitting the landed native entry shapes (`py` 1-arg `run-main`, `js` 1-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with request stream) alongside the Clojure resolver-bearing 2-arg shape; (H3) ONE derivation record (frontend/lowerer revision, descriptor, resolved runtime closure, input, output), pins reconciled by module symbol before lowering, dependency-first installation in linked composition, resolver derivation in provenance / live cell in the task; (H4) complete effect-unwind traversal per frame kind with exactly-once cleanup, a P2′ cold-error policy for plain `yang.clojure`, `clojure.core.impl` owning zero cells while declaring its runtime effects; (H5) address-bound export-**role** evidence (same-arity wrong-role fails closed); (H6) the §5.1 example labeled a Track B recipe recording bundled shape, linked trailing forms, pins, and C1 behavior independently; (H7) slice repair — P1′ clj-only synthetic fixtures, P2′ native collection invocation + bundled shadowing, P3′ the real cross-syntax unwind; (H8) boxed conversion/true-division at the host boundary, zero-raw-double scoped to boxed-path profiles; (M9) `yang.core.defquoted` naming consistency, r6 gates attached verbatim to Track B, oracle assignment (legacy pins ← native oracles, default ← capability refusals); (R) default-profile regressions — unqualified `:k` admission, cross-carrier integer identity, `:clj/unbound` distinguishability, canonical order settled to Jing encoded-byte order.\n16:- **2026-11-21 (r6 → r7 Clojure-First Default & Legacy Track, plus landed-DRY reconciliation):** Three owner directives. **(D10) Default-profile inversion:** for `yang.python` (and later `yang.typescript`/`yang.php`), the **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** runtime profile; the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` semantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist, oracle-parity-proven, at their current content addresses), with their *re-architecture* onto `yrt.*`/boxed float deferred until legacy demand justifies it. **(Clojure-first roadmap):** the implementation order re-sequenced so the Clojure prelude family (`yrt.effect`/`yrt.int` with Clojure-only consumers, unified trusted `clj`, `clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core` facade, `clj.py`, the python lowerer's descriptor parameterization) is built FIRST — the other-language native preludes are untouched by those slices (zero golden churn; defquoted consolidation and emitter standardization for py/ts/php defer to the legacy track). **(DRY-alignment reconciliation):** §5.2 admission checks home in `yang.core.prelude-admission` (3→5 publics, at bound) keeping `yang.core.prelude` pure emission; §8.2 names both the guest linker modules (`yrt.*`) and their host emitter namespaces (`src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`) and acknowledges the analyzer's 3 self-loop warnings (macro self-reference, no multi-node cycles); defquoted consolidation accounted against the public-surface ledger; §2 gains the tao-architecture second-axiom alignment (the semantics descriptor is stream-resident interpreter configuration; the provenance tuple names the interpreter).\n18:**Authority:** Subordinate to [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md) (axioms, invariants, streams, host boundaries), [`adr/0004-external-effects-are-interpreted-stream-deposits.md`](./adr/0004-external-effects-are-interpreted-stream-deposits.md) (external effects as stream deposits), [`yang.antlr.md`](./yang.antlr.md) (§3 frontend SPI, §8.1–§8.2 semantic placement, §8.5.5 float addresses, §8.5.6 linked modules, §8.10 shared calling convention, §8.11 cells, §9 four-layer stdlib model), [`yang.typescript.md`](./yang.typescript.md) (§2.2 shared rulings, §17 lift enumeration, §19 owner decision A12.5), [`yang.php.md`](./yang.php.md) (§9 prelude inventory), [`yin.vm.linker.md`](./yin.vm.linker.md), [`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`](./yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md), [`dao.jing.cbor.md`](./dao.jing.cbor.md), and [`src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md`](../../src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/state.md).\n98:   - **No descriptor hook or source-facing ambient projection** may expose `cell/dsg__*`, `dsg__*`, `yin/def`, `*.rt/*`, `*.b/*`, `yang.safepoint/*`, or non-projectable internal implementation modules such as `*.impl/*` (`clojure.core.impl/*`) (`§6.3`).\n99:   - Retained protocol-condition provenance (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10.7) resides strictly inside trusted Layer-2b runtime modules (`py`, `js`, `php`, **`clj`**) in **both** bundled (`uast`) and linked (`module-uast`) emission, never exported and never exposed across `yrt.*`, Layer-2c libraries, or source scope.\n180:     - Division/floor/power: `floor` (total IEEE double floor), `floor-int` (exact integer for finite `|x| < 2^53`, else `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`), `fmod-pos` (Sterbenz remainder for finite `x >= 0, y > 0`), `floordiv-mod` (returns `[q r]` boxed pair or `:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, preserving `-0.0` quotient sign and `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0` rounding correction), `fpow-half` (half-power squaring for `py`/`js`/`clj.py`), `fpow-base` (base squaring for `php`, preserving `1.1 ** 6` bit-exact oracle parity — see D7), `neg-pow` (`[x n pow-order]`, returns boxed `float64` or `:yin.vm.float/underflow`), `parts` (`[mantissa exp2]` exact integer pair).\n187:Remains unchanged at `src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc` (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10): structural callable discovery (`entry`, `eligible?`), invocation records (`invocation`, `invocation-with`, `valid-invocation?`), and condition transfer (`condition`, `thrown`, `transfer`, `invoke`, `invoke-with`). Requires no `yrt.*` module so `yang.call` stays a leaf dependency.\n306:2. **Export collision rule (qualified vs. projected):** Distinct Layer-2a/2b/2c modules may share bare local export names across qualified module borders; collisions are refused on duplicate linker module symbols, duplicate stripped local `module-definitions` keys, or duplicate source-facing `:ambient-projections` aliases (`§6.3`).\n321:2. **Native language profiles (`py`, `js`, `php` — the Legacy compatibility track, built later):** Preserve full, faithful CPython/Node/PHP semantics for existing libraries and code that assumes them. The landed preludes already provide this at their current content addresses and remain the regression net (their oracle suites keep passing untouched). What defers is their *re-architecture* onto `yrt.*`/boxed float — a separate legacy-modernization track, undertaken only when legacy demand justifies it. Until then they run exactly as landed: frozen mechanisms, zero golden churn, selectable by pinning their revision.\n336:### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n468:### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and parameterization\n474:     - **Hooks & executable `:literals.*` targets:** must be namespace-qualified, exported by a module in the selected closure (or required host module checked against `:yin.k/arities`), and defined as a `:lambda`. **Signature vs. call shapes (r8):** admission verifies the export's verified signature against the frontend contract's **recorded entry contract**, which states the export's parameter list AND the permitted emitted call shapes (e.g. the frozen PHP `php/run-main` is a 4-parameter lambda legitimately called with 2 or 4 operands; the `clj.py` profile always takes 2 args) — a call shape outside the contract's permitted set fails. Both PHP modes are gated, including observable stream output.\n481:6. **Frontend parameterization:** `yang.python.antlr.lower`, `yang.typescript.antlr.lower`, and `yang.php.antlr.lower` read literals, hooks (including 2-arg `:unit/run-main [body-fn ambient-resolver]` and optional `:comp/finish`), capabilities, and projections from `:yang.semantics/descriptor`, preserving full CPython/Node/PHP oracle and 4-host parity under the legacy pins. **Entry-lowering contracts (r8):** each frontend's contract specifies BOTH entry shapes — the landed native entry shape (`py/run-main` 1-arg, `js` single-operand, `php` 2-or-4 with the request stream in slot two) for the legacy track, and the Clojure profile's resolver-bearing 2-arg `[body-fn ambient-resolver]` shape — so the native mapping is 1:1 against the FROZEN exports and never re-arches them to satisfy the Clojure profile. **Oracle assignment (r8):** native-oracle parity suites gate the LEGACY pins; capability-refusal suites gate the default profile.\n554:### 7.4 Unified trusted `clj` callable bridge, cross-unit admission, and §8.10.7 validation\n556:Under the Owner Clean-Slate Directive, all Clojure-family §8.10.7 callable/provenance bridging is unified directly into **trusted Layer-2b `clj`** (`src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc`, requiring `yang.call` and `yrt.effect`) — eliminating both any separate `clj.bridge` module and `yang.clojure`'s legacy `dsg__call_token` / inline provenance code in P3:\n562:- **Full 4-step §8.10.7 entry boundary:**\n609:### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n636:Per the Owner Clean-Slate Directive, regenerate affected golden snapshots cleanly per slice (`P0`–`P4`) and validate correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and CPython/Node/PHP language-oracle parity suites.\n646:| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` across all 4 hosts); consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.defquoted` (dedicated host macro namespace, keeping `yang.core.prelude` at 11 publics — naming per r8 M9, consistent across §8.1/§8.2); base-prelude emitter recipes record the *current* per-prelude modes as migration truth (`:linear` for `py`, `:balanced` for `php`/`js`; the bundled `yang.clojure` continuation family is a LEFT FOLD, not balanced — recorded as its own mode so the freeze is exact) without changing shapes. | No golden churn for py/js/php (no shape change); new modules get fresh addresses | Closure, missing-manifest, `host-limits`, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint tests; 4-host test suite for `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`), `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries`, and `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 -> :underflow`, `format` `1.0 -> \"1.0\"`); existing py/php oracle suites unchanged-green. |\n649:| **P3′ — Descriptor parameterization + `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (the DEFAULT flip)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation; define the python frontend contract; refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` (the legacy `py-v1` descriptor pins today's `'py/*` hooks 1:1 — behavior-preserving, gated by the existing CPython oracle suites); publish `clj.py`; flip `yang.python`'s default `runtime-profile` to `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (a revision re-pin in `yang.frontend`). | py goldens regenerate under the descriptor-driven path (legacy descriptor byte-identical outcomes); clojure-core-v1 gets fresh goldens | Legacy-descriptor behavior preservation: full CPython corpus + 4-host parity under `py-v1` pin; end-to-end 4-host `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` suite (numeric/float ops, `:max-bits 53` limit traps, `data/admit-key?` refusals, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-entries` ordering, deterministic `str`/`gensym`); the cross-syntax `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind gate — cleanup and context restoration, exactly once per activation — listed directly here; capability refusal tests (typed `except E:`, `genexpr` under `:control/generators :refused`); default-profile regressions (r8): an unqualified `:k` key admits successfully (the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only); equal exact integers in different host carriers hit the same map entry on insert AND lookup; a local/projected value equal to `:clj/unbound` remains distinguishable from an absent binding; canonical traversal order matches Jing encoded-byte order (`0` before `nil`); UAST-derived validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, unqualified hooks, reserved doors, out-of-closure exports. |\n650:| **P4′ — Additional N → 1 profiles** | `:yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1` next (descriptor + ts frontend contract); `:yang.php/clojure-core-v1` after. | Fresh goldens per profile | End-to-end parity suites per profile. |\n651:| **Track B — Legacy prelude re-architecture (deferred, on demand)** | Migrate the native `py`/`js`/`php` preludes onto `yrt.effect`/`yrt.int`/boxed float (the r6 P1/P4 legs: 4→5-slot contexts, generators via `:gen/yield`, `yrt.safepoint`, `php.sp` integration per its own hooks); undertaken only when legacy demand justifies it. | Refresh py/js/php goldens per migration slice | The r6 P1/P4 gates apply verbatim at that time, attached here by value: generator + safepoint parity suites across VMs/hosts preserving PHP lifecycle/cleanup and Python `:base` rebasing; migration of `py`/`js`/`php` onto `yrt.effect`, `yrt.int`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` (4→5-slot contexts; `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` for bundled `clj`); existing Python & PHP generator tests green; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n657:1. **D10 — Default-profile policy & legacy-track deferral (`Settled — r7 Owner Directive`):** For the parameterized frontends, the **Yin/Clojure profile is the DEFAULT** (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` first; ts/php to follow); the native preludes (`py`/`js`/`php` semantics) become the **Legacy compatibility track** — kept frozen as landed (they already exist at their current content addresses with passing oracle suites), with their `yrt.*`/boxed-float re-architecture deferred to Track B until legacy demand justifies it. The clojure prelude family is built first. Consequence named in §6.1: capability refusals (classes, generators, typed `except`, `with`, kwargs) are the default experience for source written against native semantics; pinning the legacy revision is the escape hatch.\n665:   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Retain `{:py/float x}` behind a 2-line `py` boundary adapter around boxed `yin.vm.float` through P1 so Python's `1 == 1.0` oracle semantics stay cleanly isolated.\n668:   - Settled in favor of clean golden regeneration per slice (`P0`–`P4`), preserving correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and language-oracle suites rather than frozen-quirk backwards compatibility.\n675:   - *Option A (Recommended for P0/P1 — Architect concurred):* Export both `float/fpow-half` and `float/fpow-base` in `yin.vm.float` so `1.1 ** 6` preserves bit-exact parity (`0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for `py`/`js` vs `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for `php`) across existing CPython/Node and PHP language oracles.\n676:   - *Option B:* Explicitly approve unifying PHP onto `fpow-half` (or `py`/`js` onto `fpow-base`) and update the affected language's oracle departure ledger.\n.\n..\n.cljstyle\n.flutter-plugins-dependencies\n.git\n.gitignore\n.