{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,55p' test/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc\nsed -n '1,55p' test/yang/php/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc\ntail -25 /tmp/dw-p4php-node-build.log\ntail -25 /tmp/dw-p4php-deps.log\ntail -25 /tmp/dw-p4php-legacy.log\nsed -n '855,886p' docs/design/yang.php.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.antlr.portable-harness\n  \"What the JVM, Node and Dart lanes share: the host composition the PHP\n   profile runs over, the `packet` helper that builds a CST packet from a\n   nested form, and a parserless run of a packet on the AST walker.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    [dao.stream.memory-log :as memory-log]\n    [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n    [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    [yin.vm.data :as data]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(def ^:private capability-secret \"yin.vm.test-utils/capability-secret\")\n\n\n(defn make-stream\n  \"The composition's stream constructor: a deterministic ring buffer, answering\n   the create outcome the engine consumes. The lifecycle streams below come\n   from this same constructor, so request consumption and response/diagnostic\n   emission travel composition-supplied streams rather than vectors.\"\n  ([] (make-stream nil))\n  ([capacity]\n   (ringbuffer/create!\n     {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type,\n      ringbuffer/capacity-key (or capacity vm/default-stream-capacity)})))\n\n\n(defn- check-ok!\n  [result what]\n  (when-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome result))\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"PHP lifecycle stream failed: \" what) {:result result})))\n  result)\n\n\n(defn- lifecycle-stream\n  \"One open lifecycle stream handle from the composition's own constructor.\"\n  [what]\n  (:dao.stream/handle (check-ok! (make-stream) what)))\n\n\n(defn create-vm\n  \"An AST walker composed with the harness's deterministic ring-buffer stream.\"\n  ([] (create-vm {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (ast-walker/create-vm\n     (merge {:make-stream (fn [capacity] (make-stream capacity)),\n             :capability-secret capability-secret}\n            opts))))\n(ns yang.php.antlr.lower-portable-test\n  \"The lowering on every host from checked-in CST packets: no parser needed,\n   so this runs on the JVM and on Node, and on Dart except the two\n   packet-running fixtures gated below. Covers a golden, the refusal and\n   unhandled-rule diagnostics, tree validation, the stage transform's\n   routing, and every portable fixture run on the AST walker.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.packets :as packets]\n    [yang.php.antlr.packets-p3b :as packets-p3b]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as h]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs :as programs]\n    [yang.php.antlr.programs-p3b :as p3b]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n\n\n(def ^:private echo-1\n  (h/packet [:htmlDocument\n             [:phpBlock\n              [:topStatement\n               [:statement\n                [:echoStatement\n                 [\"Echo\" \"echo\"]\n                 [:expressionList\n                  [:expression\n                   [:constant [:literalConstant [:numericConstant [\"Decimal\" \"1\"]]]]]]\n                 [\"SemiColon\" \";\"]]]]]\n             [\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\"]]))\n\n\n(deftest hand-packet-golden-test\n  (is (= (u/app (u/v 'php/echo) (u/app (u/v 'php/to-string) (u/lit 1)))\n         (lower/lower-module-body echo-1))))\n\n\n(defn- diagnostic\n  [pk]\n  (try (lower/lower-module-body pk)\n       nil\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo :cljs ExceptionInfo) e\n         (select-keys (ex-data e) [:yang.php/diagnostic :rule :construct]))))\n\n\n(deftest unknown-rule-fails-qualified-test\n  (is (= {:yang.php/diagnostic :yang.php/unhandled-rule, :rule \"noSuchRule\"}\n         (diagnostic (h/packet [:htmlDocument [:phpBlock [:noSuchRule]]\n                                [\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\"]])))))\n\n\n(deftest unsupported-rule-names-its-construct-test\n  (is (= {:yang.php/diagnostic :yang.php/unsupported,\n          :rule \"gotoStatement\",\n          :construct :goto}\n         (diagnostic (h/packet [:htmlDocument\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n[:test] Compiling ...\n  yin.vm.ucf.authority.grant (in:2, out:7)\n  yin.vm.ucf.authority.input (in:3, out:4)\n  yin.vm.ucf.compose (in:1, out:11)\n  yin.vm.ucf.custody (in:12, out:1)\n  yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver (in:1, out:17)\n  yin.vm.ucf.holder.export (in:1, out:5)\n  yin.vm.ucf.holder.reader (in:1, out:9)\n  yin.vm.ucf.holder.writer (in:1, out:7)\n  yin.vm.ucf.ledger (in:8, out:5)\n  yin.vm.ucf.remote (in:2, out:5)\n  yin.vm.ucf.rows (in:4, out:14)\n  yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint (in:5, out:3)\n  yin.vm.values (in:12, out:3)\n\n✓ No tightly coupled clusters (SCCs size > 1)\n\n=== RECOMMENDATIONS ===\n\n2. Reduce high-degree nodes:\n   - These namespaces have too many responsibilities\n   - Analyze internal clusters and extract into separate namespaces\n   - Minimize public API to essential entry points\n\n\nFor detailed guidance, see docs/agents/malleability.md\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yang.php.antlr.e2e-test\n|    |                                    | `ArgumentCountError: f(): Argument |\n|    |                                    | #n ($p) not passed`; the variadic  |\n|    |                                    | array holds the trailing           |\n|    |                                    | positionals, then the string-keyed |\n|    |                                    | unknown named arguments in send    |\n|    |                                    | order                              |\n+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\n| 64 | positional argument after a named  | compile-time `Error: Cannot use    |\n|    | one                                | positional argument after named    |\n|    |                                    | argument`, a                       |\n|    |                                    | `:yang.php/compile-error`          |\n|    |                                    | diagnostic                         |\n+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\n| 65 | spread with string keys,           | each string key is a named         |\n|    | `f(...['x' => 1])`                 | argument under row 57 step 3 at    |\n|    |                                    | the spread's send; integer keys    |\n|    |                                    | are positional; a positional after |\n|    |                                    | string keys is the run-time        |\n|    |                                    | `Error: Cannot use positional      |\n|    |                                    | argument after named argument`     |\n+----+------------------------------------+------------------------------------+\n\nCost: one vector push per counted owned temporary and one release per\nstatement that produced any; scalars, strings and plain arrays never touch the\nlist.\n\n#### 4.4.3 Iteration\n\nAn instance carries `:iterators` (the iterator cells registered on it) and\n`:ptr`, its internal pointer: an index into its order vector, default 0,\nadjusted on deletes like iterator positions. An iterator holds per-table\nrecords, `{:current h :tables {h pos, h' pos ...}}`, where a position is the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
