{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_68","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '96,123p;178,223p' src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\nsed -n '1,93p' src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj\nhead -35 /tmp/dw-p4php-deps.log\ngit diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"\n\n(defn compile-tests\n  \"Compile every test namespace through the cljd tool.\"\n  [namespaces]\n  (let [exit (apply run!* \"clojure\" \"-M:clojuredart:cljd\" \"compile\"\n                    namespaces)]\n    (when-not (zero? exit)\n      (println \"cljd compile failed, exit\" exit)\n      (System/exit exit))))\n\n\n(defn shard\n  \"Greedy balanced partition of `files` into `n` groups by file size.\n   Deterministic: ties are broken by path.\"\n  [files n]\n  (let [sized (sort-by (juxt (comp - fs/size) identity) files)\n        init  (vec (repeat n {:size 0 :files []}))]\n    (->> sized\n         (reduce (fn [shards f]\n                   (let [i (first (first (sort-by\n                                           (juxt (comp :size second) first)\n                                           (map-indexed vector shards))))]\n                     (-> shards\n                         (update-in [i :size] + (fs/size f))\n                         (update-in [i :files] conj f))))\n                 init)\n         (map (comp sort :files))\n        no-compile? (some #{\"--no-compile\"} args)\n        no-run?    (some #{\"--no-run\"} args)\n        ;; individual-test selection (owner ruling 2026-11-07: the focus rule\n        ;; runs the failing TEST, not the namespace): --only accepts NS or\n        ;; NS/test-name; entries with a test name become flutter --plain-name\n        ;; filters so only the named deftests execute.\n        {only :namespaces, test-names :tests}\n        (when (some #{\"--only\"} args)\n          (let [v (second (drop-while #(not= \"--only\" %) args))\n                entries (vec (remove str/blank? (str/split (str v) #\",\")))]\n            {:namespaces (vec (distinct (map #(first (str/split % #\"/\")) entries)))\n             :tests (vec (keep #(when (str/includes? % \"/\")\n                                  (last (str/split % #\"/\")))\n                               entries))}))\n        wanted     (cond only only\n                         slow-only? (slow-namespaces)\n                         :else (test-namespaces))]\n    (when (empty? wanted)\n      (println \"No test namespaces selected.\")\n      (System/exit 1))\n    (when-not no-compile?\n      (compile-tests (or only (test-namespaces))))\n    (let [files (filter fs/exists? (map dart-file wanted))\n          missing (remove (comp fs/exists? dart-file) wanted)]\n      (when (seq missing)\n        (let [jvm-only (if (and only (not slow-only?))\n                         (filter jvm-only? missing)\n                         [])\n              fatal (remove (set jvm-only) missing)]\n          (when (seq jvm-only)\n            (println \"JVM-only namespaces (compiled, no Dart tests; skipped):\"\n                     (str/join \", \" jvm-only)))\n          (when (seq fatal)\n            (println \"No generated Dart test for:\" (str/join \", \" fatal))\n            (when (or slow-only? only)\n              (System/exit 1)))))\n      (when (empty? files)\n        (println \"No generated test files found.\")\n        (System/exit 1))\n      (let [shards (write-shards! files shard-dir)]\n        (if no-run?\n          (do (println (format \"Emitted %d test files in %d shards under %s\"\n                               (count files) (count shards) shard-dir))\n              (System/exit 0))\n          (do (println (format \"Running %d test files in %d shards\"\n                               (count files) (count shards)))\n;; The jolt test runner (yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §11; J1), run UNDER\n;; jolt:\n;;\n;;   . build/tools/jolt-env.sh\n;;   \"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj NS...\n;;   \"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj --self-test\n;;\n;; How it finds the tests: it does not scan. The namespaces are the explicit\n;; command-line list (bb test:jolt-host passes the four dao.host oracle\n;; namespaces), and each is loaded by `require` through jolt's own source-root\n;; search, which the aliases set: :jolt replaces the paths with src/jolt,\n;; src/cljc, src/clj (src/jolt first, so a host override there wins) and\n;; :jolt-test adds test (the oracle) and src/dev (this runner and its\n;; sentinel). jolt resolves :extra-paths roots BEFORE the :replace-paths\n;; ones (`jolt -Srepro -Spath -A:jolt:jolt-test`: test, src/dev, src/jolt,\n;; src/cljc, src/clj); neither test nor src/dev holds a dao/host source, so\n;; the override order is unaffected. Fixture files the tests read\n;; (test/resources/...) are relative to the working directory, the\n;; repository root.\n;;\n;; Per namespace: a load failure is counted and reported, and the run goes on.\n;; Per test var, in source order: each runs through clojure.test/test-var,\n;; which reports an escaping throw as an :error, inside a second guard of this\n;; runner's own, so a throwing test never aborts the batch. Totals are tests,\n;; assertions (pass + fail + error), failures, errors and load failures; the\n;; exit status is nonzero when any of the last three is.\n;;\n;; --self-test runs the sentinel namespace jolt-runner-sentinel (a passing\n;; test, a test that throws, then a passing test) and exits 0 only when the\n;; runner counted exactly that: 3 tests, 1 error, and the test after the\n;; throwing one ran.\n(ns jolt-test-runner\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :as t]))\n\n\n;; Lane B: the child reports which host scheme launched it (silent when\n;; JOLT_TARGET is unset, so legacy invocations keep their output\n;; byte-identical).\n(when-let [t (System/getenv \"JOLT_TARGET\")] (println (str \"jolt-target: \" t)))\n\n\n(defn- tally\n  []\n  (select-keys @t/counters [:test :pass :fail :error]))\n\n\n(defn- delta\n  [before after]\n  (merge-with - after before))\n\n\n(defn- test-vars-of\n  \"The test vars of namespace `ns-sym` in source order.\"\n  [ns-sym]\n  (->> (vals (ns-interns ns-sym))\n       (filter #(:test (meta %)))\n       (sort-by #(or (:line (meta %)) 0))))\n\n\n(defn- run-ns\n  \"Run namespace `ns-sym`; answers {:ns :load-error :counts :tests}.\"\n  [ns-sym]\n  (let [loaded (try\n                 (require ns-sym)\n                 nil\n                 (catch Throwable e e))]\n    (if loaded\n      {:ns ns-sym :load-error (str (ex-message loaded)) :counts {} :tests []}\n      (let [before (tally)\n            per-test (mapv (fn [v]\n                             (let [b (tally)]\n                               (try\n                                 (t/test-vars [v])\n                                 (catch Throwable e\n                                   ;; test-var already guards; this is the\n                                   ;; runner's own floor\n                                   (t/do-report {:type :error\n                                                 :message \"escaped test-vars\"\n                                                 :expected nil :actual e})))\n                               [(:name (meta v)) (delta b (tally))]))\n                           (test-vars-of ns-sym))]\n        {:ns ns-sym\n         :load-error nil\n         :counts (delta before (tally))\n         :tests per-test}))))\n\n\n(defn- assertions\n  [c]\n  (+ (:pass c 0) (:fail c 0) (:error c 0)))\n\n\nWARNING: Implicit use of clojure.main with options is deprecated, use -M ./bin/analyze-deps.clj\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\nGenerating dependency graph...\n\n=== DEPENDENCY COUPLING ANALYSIS ===\n\n✓ No circular dependencies detected\n\n⚠ HIGH-DEGREE NODES (144 namespaces with 6+ connections)\n  dao.await (in:1, out:6)\n  dao.data (in:5, out:2)\n  dao.datom (in:12, out:0)\n  dao.gui.event (in:3, out:6)\n  dao.gui.event.pointer (in:1, out:5)\n  dao.host.bytes (in:22, out:0)\n  dao.