{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_238","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented P4′-b on `feat/p4-php-clojure-core` at `0c36043d`. The work is uncommitted, and all four new files are marked intent-to-add. **The new profile passed on JVM and Node. The broader legacy oracle runs are still open.**\n\n### Implementation\n\n- [profiles.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4php/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/profiles.cljc) publishes and verifies the `php-v1` and `clojure-core-v1` descriptors and runtime closures.\n- [contract.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4php/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/contract.cljc) and [semantics.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4php/src/cljc/yang/core/semantics.cljc) validate the fixed hook ABI, address-bound roles, and entry shapes. The frozen `php/run-main` accepts **2 and 4 operands**, with the request stream in slot two. A **3-operand** call returns `:arity`. `clj.php/run-main` takes `[body-fn ambient-resolver]`.\n- [lower.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4php/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc) reads literals, hooks, and capabilities from the descriptor. Refused constructs produce diagnostics before any program batch is emitted.\n- [clj_runtime.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4php/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/clj_runtime.cljc) delegates callable creation and invocation to `clj`, installs the cold-error policy, and emits body records on the attached response stream. The gate checks bundled and linked execution, including zero records for empty output.\n- [frontend.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4php/src/cljc/yang/frontend.cljc) and [frontends.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4php/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc) select `clojure-core-v1` by default, accept an explicit `php-v1` pin, and retain the binding captured by an in-flight request. [descriptor_profile_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4php/test/yang/php/antlr/descriptor_profile_test.cljc) covers those paths and the new goldens.\n\nThe profile follows §6.4’s “4-parameter lambda legitimately called with 2 or 4 operands” and applies the §6.5 default at catalog selection. Bare compiler calls use `php-v1`, which keeps the existing oracle entry points on their native pin. On Node, the profile restores the float kind of one `1e15` literal when reconstructing the pinned artifact. The resulting manifest matches the frozen JVM address, and the PHP prelude files are untouched. [r8 design](/Users/sto/workspace/dw-p4php/docs/design/yang.preludes.md:437)\n\n### Verification\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---:|\n| JVM PHP profile | 6 tests, 320 assertions, zero failures or errors |\n| Node PHP profile | 6 tests, 320 assertions, zero failures or errors |\n| Node profile and legacy portable suites | 55 tests, 2,537 assertions, zero failures or errors |\n| JVM legacy portable, prelude, and request-stream suites | 44 tests, 1,662 assertions, zero failures or errors |\n| Dart portable suites | 48 tests passed |\n| Jolt/Chez portable profile | 2 tests, 20 assertions, zero failures or errors |\n| Legacy lowering against `0c36043d` | 1,325 fixtures, zero differences, including 518 quick permutations and 271 PHPT cases |\n| Dependency analysis | Zero cycles and zero multi-namespace SCCs |\n\n```sh\nclj -J-Xmx4g -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.descriptor-profile-test\nclj -J-Xmx3g -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge '{:autorun false :ns-regexp \"^yang[.]php[.]antlr[.]descriptor-profile-test$\"}'\nnode target/node-tests.js --test=yang.php.antlr.descriptor-profile-test\n\nclj -J-Xmx3g -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test --config-merge '{:autorun false :ns-regexp \"^yang[.]php[.]antlr[.](descriptor-profile|lower-portable|prelude|class-model)-test$\"}'\nnode target/node-tests.js --test=yang.php.antlr.descriptor-profile-test,yang.php.antlr.lower-portable-test,yang.php.antlr.prelude-test,yang.php.antlr.class-model-test\n\nclj -J-Xmx3g -M:test -n yang.php.antlr.lower-portable-test -n yang.php.antlr.prelude-test -n yang.php.antlr.request-context-test\nbb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --only yang.php.antlr.descriptor-profile-test,yang.php.antlr.lower-portable-test,yang.php.antlr.prelude-test,yang.php.antlr.class-model-test\nbuild/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-test src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj yang.php.antlr.descriptor-profile-test\nclj -J-Xmx4g -Sdeps '{:aliases {:php-baseline {:extra-paths [\"build/php-baseline\" \"test\"]}}}' -M:php-baseline build/php-baseline/quick_legacy_parity.clj\nclj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj\n```\n\nDart and Jolt used parserless CST fixtures. The wider JVM legacy runs were still executing `yang.php.antlr.e2e-test` at the last check and had no final counts. A separate comparison that included the full permutation corpus exhausted a 3 GiB heap inside ANTLR. The optional full permutation oracle file is absent from this checkout. [Full legacy run](/tmp/dw-p4php-legacy.log) · [Quick legacy run](/tmp/dw-p4php-legacy-quick.log) · [Completed parity comparison](/tmp/dw-p4php-quick-baseline.log)\n\nThe optional Python/catalog regression ran 19 tests and 148 assertions. Its three errors reproduced the documented legacy Python pin mismatch. [Regression log](/tmp/dw-p4php-selector-regression.log)\n\nCodex session `01a20916-72fb-7eb0-8080-e7904ff4d969`."}}
